# Scoped ai-script blocks

This fixture demonstrates an `ai-script` block split into two
explicitly-scoped sub-blocks (`public` and `internal`). The loader
surfaces both blocks; consumers are expected to filter at runtime
based on the agent's tenant identity.

Useful as a starting point for documenting scope filtering patterns
without prescribing a specific filter implementation.
